i><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-xiao-of-zhou"><span class="enc-name">King Xiao of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Xiao of Zhou was a king of the Western Zhou dynasty in the early 9th century BCE, conventionally dated c. 891–886 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-xie-of-zhou"><span class="enc-name">King Xie of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Xie of Zhou, personal name Yuchen, was a rival king set up after the fall of the Western Zhou capital in 771 BCE, in opposition to King Ping.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-xuan-of-zhou"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/king-xuan-of-zhou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King Xuan of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Xuan of Zhou was the eleventh king of the Western Zhou dynasty, who came to the throne after the Gonghe regency.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-yan-of-song"><span class="enc-name">King Yan of Song</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Yan of Song was the last ruler of the state of Song in the Warring States period, taking power around 328 BCE and later assuming the royal title.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-you-of-zhou"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/king-you-of-zhou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King You of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King You of Zhou was the last king of the Western Zhou dynasty, reigning from 781 to 771 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-zhao-of-chu"><span class="enc-name">King Zhao of Chu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Zhao of Chu ruled the State of Chu from 516 to 489 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-zhao-of-zhou"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/king-zhao-of-zhou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King Zhao of Zhou</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Zhao of Zhou was the fourth king of the Western Zhou dynasty, reigning in the late tenth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-zhaoxiang-of-qin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/king-zhaoxiang-of-qin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King Zhaoxiang of Qin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Zhaoxiang of Qin ruled the State of Qin from 306 to 251 BCE, the longest reign of the Warring States period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/king-zhuang-of-chu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/king-zhuang-of-chu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King Zhuang of Chu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">King Zhuang of Chu (reigned 613–591 BCE) was a ruler of the State of Chu, counted among the Five Hegemons of the Spring and Autumn period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kings-law"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kings-law.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">King's Law</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The King's Law (Kongeloven, or Lex Regia) was the fundamental law of absolute monarchy in Denmark-Norway, signed by King Frederick III in 1665 and published in 1709.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-alo"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Alo</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="e