-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Jerusalem</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Jerusalem was a Crusader state established in the Levant after the First Crusade captured Jerusalem in 1099.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kanem"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Kanem</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Kanem was a state to the north-east of Lake Chad, ruled by the Sayfawa dynasty, which converted to Islam around the eleventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-kongo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Kongo</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Kongo was a Central African state centred on Mbanza Kongo in present-day northern Angola, flourishing from the fourteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Lombardy–Venetia</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Lombardy–Venetia was a crown land of the Austrian Empire created by the Congress of Vienna in 1815 from the former Duchy of Milan and Republic of Venice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Luang Phrabang</spa