 has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Portugal</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Portugal was a monarchy on the Atlantic coast of Iberia, formed during the Reconquista against the Almoravid and Almohad states.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Prussia</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Prussia was a German state ruled by the Hohenzollern dynasty from 1701, known for its efficient bureaucracy and powerful army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-sigave"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Sigave</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigave is one of the two traditional kingdoms of the island of Futuna in Wallis and Futuna, covering the western part of the island around the village of Leava.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-sine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-sine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Sine</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Sine was a Serer kingdom in present-day Senegal, located in the region dominated by the Jolof Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-strathclyde"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-strathclyde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Strathclyde</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Strathclyde was a Brittonic kingdom of the early medieval north, centred first on Dumbarton Rock, called Alt Clut, and after a Viking siege of 870 on…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-the-lombards.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of the Lombards</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of the Lombards was a Germanic kingdom established in Italy after the Lombard invasion of 568.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of the Netherlands</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of the Netherlands is the Dutch monarchy established in 1815 after the Napoleonic Wars, succeeding the Dutch Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of the Two Sicilies was the largest state of pre-unification Italy, formed in 1816 when the Bourbon king Ferdinand I merged the kingdoms of Naples and Sicily.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-tylis"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Tylis</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Tylis was a Celtic state in eastern Thrace founded by Gauls under Comontorius after the Celtic invasion of the Balkans in 279 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia was a state built by the Amorite ruler Shamshi-Adad I in northern Mesopotamia in the early second millennium BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-zimbabwe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingdom-of-zimbabwe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingdom of Zimbabwe</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kingdom of Zimbabwe was the state centred on Great Zimbabwe on the Zimbabwe plateau, which flourished from about the twelfth to the fifteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingisepp"><span class="enc-name">Kingisepp</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingisepp is a town in Leningrad Oblast, Russia, on the Luga River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingkitsarat"><span class="enc-name">Kingkitsarat</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingkitsarat was the first king of Luang Phrabang, ruling from 1707 to 1713.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingkitsarath"><span class="enc-name">Kingkitsarath</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingkitsarath was the first king of Luang Prabang, a grandson of King Sourigna Vongsa of Lan Xang.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingston-jamaica"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingston-jamaica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingston, Jamaica</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingston is the capital and largest city of Jamaica, on a deep natural harbour on the south-east coast.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingston-ontario"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingston-ontario.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingston, Ontario</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingston is a city in Ontario, Canada, at the eastern end of Lake Ontario where it flows into the St. Lawrence River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kingstown"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kingstown.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kingstown</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kingstown is the capital and chief port of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, on the south-west coast of Saint Vincent.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinkaku-ji"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinkaku-ji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kinkaku-ji</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Kinkaku-ji, the Temple of the Golden Pavilion, is a Zen temple in northern Kyoto, Japan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinmen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinmen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kinmen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kinmen, also called Quemoy, is a group of islands governed by the Republic of China (Taiwan) lying only a few kilometres off the city of Xiamen in mainland China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kinnaird-head"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kinnaird-head.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kinnaird Head</span><span class="e